# PaalStack Next.js Starter Conventions

This is an **application** that **consumes** the `@paalstack/react-ui` design system. You are building app features, not authoring library components. The library already provides Button, Card, Form, Dialog, DataTable, Select, Tabs, Toast, and 70+ more — search it before creating anything.

Source of the design system: https://github.com/paalamugan/paalstack-react-ui

---

## Imports

```tsx
// UI components — from the umbrella package
import { Button, Card, Form, Box, HStack, TypographyH1, TypographyMuted, toast } from '@paalstack/react-ui';

// Server-safe utilities — from the /lib sub-path
import { cn, logger } from '@paalstack/react-ui/lib';

// Hooks — client-only, separate package
import { useDisclosure, useLocalStorage } from '@paalstack/react-hooks';

// Icons — ALWAYS from a family sub-path, never the root barrel
import { LuSettings, LuMoon, LuSun } from '@paalstack/react-icons/lu';
```

### Icons

- Import from a family sub-path: `/lu` (Lucide, default) · `/hi2` · `/fa6` · `/tb` · `/md` · `/ri` · `/bi` · `/bs` · `/fi` · `/io5` · `/rx` · `/si` · `/pi` · `/vsc` · `/go`.
- Never `import { LuUser } from '@paalstack/react-icons'` (root barrel).
- Never install `lucide-react`, `heroicons`, or `react-icons` directly — the sub-path exists.

### Never use native HTML elements in JSX

Replace native tags with PaalStack components:

```tsx
// ❌ Native HTML — never use these
<div> <header> <main> <section> <nav> <footer> <aside> <article>
<h1> <h2> <h3> <h4> <h5> <h6> <p> <span> <strong> <ul> <ol> <li> <code> <blockquote> <button>

// ✅ Layout — Box + semantic `as` prop
<Box as="header" />   // <header>
<Box as="main" />     // <main>
<Box as="section" />  // <section>
<Box as="nav" />      // <nav>
<Box as="footer" />   // <footer>

// ✅ Typography — named exports (NOT Typography.* namespace — undefined in Turbopack)
<TypographyH1 /> <TypographyH2 /> <TypographyH3 /> <TypographyH4 />
<TypographyH5 /> <TypographyH6 /> <TypographyP /> <TypographyStrong />
<TypographyCode /> <TypographyUL /> <TypographyOL /> <TypographyLI />
<TypographyBlockQuote /> <TypographyLead /> <TypographyMuted /> <TypographySubtle />
<TypographySmall /> <TypographyLarge />

// ✅ Heading / Text — polymorphic `as` override or inline variants
<Heading as="h2" />   // dynamic heading level
<Text as="span" />    // inline text fragment

// ✅ Button — replaces <button>
<Button />
```

### Styling

- Use semantic design tokens: `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-accent`, `bg-card`, `bg-background`, `bg-sidebar`.
- No raw hex colors when a semantic token exists.
- Extend components with `className`; merge via `cn()` from `@paalstack/react-ui/lib`.
- Dark mode is handled by `NextThemeProvider` in `src/providers/theme-provider.tsx` — test both themes.

