## Project structure (follow this pattern)

```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router routes
│   ├── layout.tsx          # Root layout — Providers + SiteHeader
│   ├── (route)/page.tsx    # Pages
│   └── api/                # Route Handlers (use withApiErrorHandling)
├── apis/                   # HTTP layer — one module per endpoint group
│   └── example/
│       ├── api.ts          # functions mapping 1:1 to endpoints
│       ├── type.ts         # request/response types
│       └── index.ts        # barrel
├── services/               # Business logic above the API layer
│   └── api/service.ts      # orchestrates apis, transforms, domain errors
├── hooks/
│   ├── queries/            # TanStack Query hooks (useXQuery)
│   │   └── useExampleQuery/{hook.ts,index.ts}
│   ├── mutations/          # TanStack Query mutations (useXMutation)
│   │   └── useExampleMutation/{hook.ts,index.ts}
│   └── useAppStore/        # Zustand store access
├── schemas/                # Zod schemas (react-hook-form + zodResolver)
│   └── example/{schema.ts,index.ts}
├── features/               # Feature-scoped modules (auth, billing, ...)
│   └── auth/{hooks,types,index.ts}
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                 # App-specific UI wrappers (EmptyState, StatCard, ...)
│   ├── shared/             # Cross-feature components (ConfirmDialog, AppErrorBoundary)
│   └── SiteHeader/         # Feature components
├── constants/              # ROUTES, app config
├── enums/                  # Status enums
├── libs/                   # Infrastructure (env, axios, query-client, logger, error, db, supabase, rbac, rate-limit)
├── providers/              # Providers composition
├── stores/                 # Zustand stores
├── types/                  # Shared types
└── utils/                  # Pure helpers
```

**Module pattern:** each module is a folder with an implementation file (`component.tsx`, `hook.ts`, `schema.ts`, `api.ts`, `store.ts`) plus an `index.ts` barrel that re-exports. Import via the barrel (`@/components/ExampleCard`, `@/hooks/queries/useExampleQuery`).

