## Errors

Use the typed error system in `src/libs/error/error.ts`:

- `AppErrorBase` hierarchy: `ValidationError`, `UnauthorizedError`, `ForbiddenError`, `NotFoundError`, `ConflictError`, `DatabaseError`, `ExternalServiceError`, `RateLimitedError`.
- Each maps to an HTTP status via `ERROR_STATUS_MAP`.
- In Route Handlers, wrap with `withApiErrorHandling` and return `apiSuccess` / `apiError`:

```tsx
import { withApiErrorHandling, apiSuccess } from '@/libs/api';
import { UnauthorizedError } from '@/libs/error';

export const GET = withApiErrorHandling(async (request: NextRequest) => {
  const { user, error } = await requireAuth();
  if (error) throw new UnauthorizedError();
  return apiSuccess(await listItems(user.id));
});
```

- Throw the typed errors; never return raw 500 HTML.

---

## Providers

- `src/providers/providers.tsx` composes `PostHogProvider` → `ThemeProvider` → `QueryProvider`.
- `ThemeProvider` wraps `NextThemeProvider` from `@paalstack/react-ui` (includes ToastProvider — no separate `<Toaster>`).
- Add new providers to `src/providers/providers.tsx`, not the root layout.

---

## Do Not

- Duplicate Button, Input, Dialog, Table, Form, Select, Checkbox, or common hooks the library provides.
- Write new `useMediaQuery`, `useLocalStorage`, `useDisclosure` — `@paalstack/react-hooks` covers them.
- Import the `@paalstack/react-icons` root barrel or install icon packages directly.
- Use raw hex colors when semantic tokens exist.
- Use native HTML elements in JSX.
- Read `process.env` directly — use `env` from `@/libs/env`.
- Mix Zustand and TanStack Query for the same data.
- Author library components here — this is a consumer app.

